<!--
  Vanilla Races Expanded - Sanguophage: what its feeding genes and its hemohunter mental state
  mean to the pads' Dismember. The fields are DismemberExtension's, their rules in
  Ability_Dismember's header; this root only names that mod's defs for them. Its 1.7 folder is
  its 1.6 one, so this root is listed under both versions.

  drainSources. That mod gives a feeding gene an ability of its own beside Bloodfeed, with the
  same 20 hemogen scaled by body size, and the drain takes each gene's targets as that ability
  does:
  - VRE_AnimalFeeder feeds on any animal. Its AnimalFeed takes blood by the animal's base body
    size, all of it from one of 0.2 or smaller and a tenth from one of 2 or larger, in a
    straight line between (CompAbilityEffect_AnimalfeederBite.BiteAmount). The curve is that
    line as factors of the drain's targetBloodLoss, 0.4499 by default (1 / 0.4499 and
    0.1 / 0.4499), so the mod setting for the blood loss scales animals with everything else.
    Both are rounded up: the first must come to no less than the severity blood loss kills
    at, or the cursor's warning of the drain, which sums as the drain does, would stop short
    of "Will kill" over an animal the drain kills.
    A rat is drained dry; an elephant hardly notices. A wild animal's revenge needs nothing
    here: the strike is damage with the pilot as instigator, which vanilla already rolls
    manhunter for (Pawn_MindState.Notify_DamageTaken, 1.6 and 1.7). AnimalFeed rolls it for a
    tame animal too; the strike keeps to vanilla, which rolls it for no animal with a faction.
  - VRE_SanguoFeeder feeds on any hemogenic human, bloodfeeders included, which the plain
    drain refuses as Bloodfeed does. Its SanguoFeed refuses a target under 10 hemogen, as
    minTargetHemogen 0.1 does: an empty target would fill the pilot all the same. The 20 it
    takes beyond the bite prices a bite on the unresisting, which a torn limb has paid.
  - VRE_CorpseFeeder feeds on a human corpse found lying, which only a hemohunter strikes
    (below): its CorpseFeed is how a pilot in its right mind feeds on one. CorpseFeed gives
    its 20 hemogen whatever blood the corpse has left and destroys it; the drain takes what
    blood is left, as from a target that died under it, and leaves the corpse. A target
    struck alive is never this source's, dead or not.

  feedingHediffs. Each of that mod's feedings leaves its hediff on the feeder and removes the
  other two, and Bloodfeed and a hemogen pack remove all three (its postfix on
  CompAbilityEffect_BloodfeederBite.Apply, its HemogenPackIngestionPatch.xml). A drain does the
  same: a source's hediff stays or is given, the rest come off.

  hemohunterStates. Its blood moon sends every hemogenic human on the map under 45 hemogen
  into VRE_Hemohunter, in which its JobGiver_Hemohunter walks the pawn to a random human
  without the hemogen gene and bites, whatever feeding genes the pawn has.
  ThinkTreeDefs/HemohunterDismember.xml asks ours first. Ours takes the nearest prey, not a
  random one, and counts as prey what the three sources above open to the pilot while the
  ability's hemohunterHuntsByGene is on.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef[defName="HPWC_Dismember"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="HemophageWarcasket.DismemberExtension"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <drainSources>
        <li>
          <pilotGene>VRE_AnimalFeeder</pilotGene>
          <target>Animal</target>
          <hediff>VRE_ConsumedAnimalHemogen</hediff>
          <bloodLossFactorByBaseBodySize>
            <points>
              <li>(0.2, 2.2228)</li>
              <li>(2, 0.2223)</li>
            </points>
          </bloodLossFactorByBaseBodySize>
        </li>
        <li>
          <pilotGene>VRE_SanguoFeeder</pilotGene>
          <target>Hemogenic</target>
          <hediff>VRE_ConsumedSanguophageHemogen</hediff>
          <minTargetHemogen>0.1</minTargetHemogen>
        </li>
        <li>
          <pilotGene>VRE_CorpseFeeder</pilotGene>
          <target>Corpse</target>
          <hediff>VRE_ConsumedCorpseHemogen</hediff>
        </li>
      </drainSources>
      <feedingHediffs>
        <li>VRE_ConsumedAnimalHemogen</li>
        <li>VRE_ConsumedCorpseHemogen</li>
        <li>VRE_ConsumedSanguophageHemogen</li>
      </feedingHediffs>
      <hemohunterStates>
        <li>VRE_Hemohunter</li>
      </hemohunterStates>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
